# Git: always commit and push to main

After completing any substantive code change in this repo:

1. Commit on `main` (do not ask for permission first).
2. Push to `origin/main` immediately after a successful commit.
3. Skip secrets, credentials, `.env*`, and build logs (`nextbuild*.log`, etc.).
4. Use a concise commit message focused on why.
5. Never force-push to main. Never amend commits that are already pushed.
6. If there is nothing meaningful to commit, do not create an empty commit.
